<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n63305" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιμν-άζω</span></b> , of the sea or rivers, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>form stagnant pools</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				352b35
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				356a7
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅσοι ποταμοὶ -άζουσιν εἰς
			ἕλη</span> rivers which <i>stagnate</i> into marshes, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				938a3
			</span></i>: impers., -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">άζει</span>
			<i>stagnant pools are left</i> in them, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				351b8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				352a5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of the blood,
				<i>to be stagnant</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>HA</u>
				513b4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				<u>UP</u>
				14.10
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> c. acc.,
				<i>form into a lake</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ ποταμὸς λ. τὰς ἀρούρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					2.98
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				8.8.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.Chr.
				11.76
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, of land, <i>to be flooded</i>, <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				1.3.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PStrassb.</u>
				10.11
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A.D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> intr. in 
				Act.
			, of a country, <i>become a marsh</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν τοῖς -άζουσι τόποις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Mete.</u>
					340b37
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				4.18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				8.5.1
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
